ession":"by accident","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「偶然に／たまたま」の主要な句表現で、by chanceとは別に会話で頻出する。"}],"after_paraphrases":["accidentally","by accident"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"canonical以外にも日常英語で極めて有用な2表現があり、MISS扱いは不適切。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01505","prompt_ja":"someoneをsomeone elseに紹介する","canonical_snapshot":"introduce someone to someone else","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["introduce someone to someone else"],"candidate_review":[],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"prompt-onlyでも主要回答はcanonicalそのもので、独立して登録すべき別表現はない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01506","prompt_ja":"すぐに","canonical_snapshot":"at once","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["immediately","right away","at once","straight away"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"immediately","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「すぐに」の最も基本的な副詞の一つで、会話・文章とも高頻度。"},{"expression":"right away","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「すぐに」の高頻度な会話表現で、独立した句として学習価値が高い。"},{"expression":"straight away","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"特に英国英語で一般的な「すぐに」の主要表現で、地域差として価値がある。"}],"after_paraphrases":["immediately","right away","straight away"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"高頻度の副詞・会話表現・主要地域variantを追加する価値が高い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01507","prompt_ja":"確かに","canonical_snapshot":"for sure","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["certainly","definitely","surely","indeed"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"certainly","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「確かに」の主要な高頻度副詞で、肯定・確信の回答として自然。"},{"expression":"definitely","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"強い確信を示す非常に高頻度な現代英語で、promptへの自然な回答。"},{"expression":"surely","decision":"REJECT","reason":"成立する場面はあるが、話者の推論・当然視を帯びやすく、無標の「確かに」より用途が偏る。"},{"expression":"indeed","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"文章語寄りだが「確かに」の代表的な確認・強調表現で、register差として学習価値がある。"}],"after_paraphrases":["certainly","definitely","indeed"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"無標の確信表現2種と文章語の主要表現を採用し、推論色の強いsurelyは外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01508","prompt_ja":"someoneの言葉を借りれば","canonical_snapshot":"as someone put it","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["in someone's words","to quote someone","in the words of someone"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"in someone's words","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「someoneの言葉を借りれば」を直接表す自然な高頻度表現。"},{"expression":"to quote someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"引用を明示する主要constructionで、同じ日本語promptへの実用的な回答。"},{"expression":"in the words of someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"人物の表現を借りる際の定型的な言い方で、文章・スピーチで有用。"}],"after_paraphrases":["in someone's words","to quote someone","in the words of someone"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"引用・言い換え導入として実際に使う3つの主要constructionを採用する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01509","prompt_ja":"成功する","canonical_snapshot":"make good","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["succeed","be successful","make it"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"succeed","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「成功する」の最も基本的で高頻度な動詞。canonicalより基本的で、MISS扱いは教育的に不適切。"},{"expression":"be successful","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"形容詞constructionによる主要表現で、会話・文章とも非常に一般的。"},{"expression":"make it","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「うまく成功する／やり遂げる」の高頻度な口語表現で、独立した学習価値が高い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["succeed","be successful","make it"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"基本動詞・形容詞construction・主要口語idiomはいずれも高価値。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01510","prompt_ja":"結局","canonical_snapshot":"in the end","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["in the end","ultimately","after all","eventually"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"ultimately","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「結局／最終的には」を表す主要な副詞で、文章・academicでも高頻度。"},{"expression":"after all","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"文脈により「結局」の意味を自然に表す重要な談話表現。"},{"expression":"eventually","decision":"REJECT","reason":"最終結果を表す場合は近いが「やがて／ついに」の時間経過が中心で、無標の「結局」にはずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["ultimately","after all"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"結果帰着を表す主要表現を採用し、時間経過中心のeventuallyは外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01511","prompt_ja":"someoneを軽蔑する","canonical_snapshot":"feel contempt for someone","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["look down on someone","despise someone","scorn someone"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"look down on someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「someoneを軽蔑する」の非常に重要な句動詞で、会話でも高頻度。"},{"expression":"despise someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"強い軽蔑を表す主要動詞で、読解・会話とも学習価値が高い。"},{"expression":"scorn someone","decision":"REJECT","reason":"成立するがdespiseより頻度・汎用性が低く、追加学習価値が相対的に小さい。"}],"after_paraphrases":["look down on someone","despise someone"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"高頻度句動詞と主要単語を採用し、低優先の同義語は増やさない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01512","prompt_ja":"someoneを笑う","canonical_snapshot":"laugh at someone","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["laugh at someone","make fun of someone","mock someone"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"make fun of someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「someoneを笑う／からかって笑いものにする」の高頻度な口語表現。"},{"expression":"mock someone","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"嘲笑する意味の主要動詞で、「someoneを笑う」の悪意ある用法に自然に対応する。"}],"after_paraphrases":["make fun of someone","mock someone"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"笑いものにする意味で高価値な口語表現と主要動詞を追加する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01513","prompt_ja":"間違える","canonical_snapshot":"make a mistake","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["make a mistake","get something wrong","be wrong"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"get something wrong","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「somethingを間違える」に自然な高頻度constructionで、一般の「間違える」にも有用。"},{"expression":"be wrong","decision":"REJECT","reason":"主に「間違っている」という状態を表し、動作としての「間違える」とは対応がずれる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["get something wrong"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"動作として自然な別constructionのみ採用し、状態表現は外す。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01514","prompt_ja":"最もsomethingしそうにない人","canonical_snapshot":"the last person to do something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["the last person to do something","the least likely person to do something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"the least likely person to do something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"日本語promptをほぼ直接表す透明な主要constructionで、canonicalのidiomatic表現理解にも役立つ。"}],"after_paraphrases":["the least likely person to do something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"意味を明示する主要constructionとして独立した学習価値が高い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01515","prompt_ja":"somethingを飛び越える","canonical_snapshot":"leap over something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["jump over something","leap over something","vault over something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"jump over something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「somethingを飛び越える」の最も基本的で高頻度な言い方。"},{"expression":"vault over something","decision":"REJECT","reason":"手や棒を使うなど特定の跳び越え方を含みやすく、一般promptには狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["jump over something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"基本表現jump overを追加し、動作様式を狭める語は登録しない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01516","prompt_ja":"somethingを怖がっている","canonical_snapshot":"be scared of something","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["be afraid of something","be scared of something","fear something"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"be afraid of something","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「somethingを怖がっている」の最も基本的な状態表現の一つ。"},{"expression":"fear something","decision":"REJECT","reason":"意味は成立するが、現在のpromptではbe afraid ofの方が一般性・回答自然さで優先され、追加価値は低い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["be afraid of something"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"高頻度な基本constructionを追加し、同義語の過剰登録は避ける。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01517","prompt_ja":"人前で","canonical_snapshot":"in public","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["in public","in front of people","publicly"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"in front of people","decision":"REJECT","reason":"意味は作れるが説明的な組合せで、独立表現としての追加学習価値が低い。"},{"expression":"publicly","decision":"REJECT","reason":"成立するが「公に」の意味にも広がり、人前でという場面性を必ずしも保たない。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"canonicalが最も直接的で、他候補は説明的または意味範囲が広い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01518","prompt_ja":"恐怖で震える","canonical_snapshot":"tremble with fear","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["tremble with fear","shake with fear","shiver with fear"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"shake with fear","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"恐怖で体が震えることを表す非常に自然で高頻度な表現。"},{"expression":"shiver with fear","decision":"REJECT","reason":"成立するが寒さによる震えの連想も強く、一般的な恐怖反応にはshakeより優先度が低い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["shake with fear"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"高頻度で無標なshake with fearを採用し、追加同義表現は絞る。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01519","prompt_ja":"根は","canonical_snapshot":"at heart","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["at heart","deep down","essentially"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"deep down","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「根は／心の奥では」の高頻度な口語表現で、canonicalとは別の重要idiom。"},{"expression":"essentially","decision":"REJECT","reason":"「本質的には」は近いが、人の内面的本質を指す「根は」より抽象範囲が広い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["deep down"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"人の本質・内面を表す主要口語idiomとしてdeep downを追加する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01520","prompt_ja":"連続ホームドラマ","canonical_snapshot":"soap opera","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["soap opera"],"candidate_review":[],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"soap operaが現代英語の定着した主要名称で、別に登録すべき高価値表現はない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01521","prompt_ja":"歩き回る","canonical_snapshot":"pace","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["walk around","wander around","roam around","pace"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"walk around","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「歩き回る」の最も一般的で透明な高頻度表現。"},{"expression":"wander around","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"目的なく歩き回る意味の主要表現で、独立した動詞価値が高い。"},{"expression":"roam around","decision":"REJECT","reason":"成立するがwander aroundと比べ追加学習価値が低く、候補過多になる。"}],"after_paraphrases":["walk around","wander around"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"一般表現と目的なく歩く主要表現を採用し、近接同義語は増やしすぎない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01522","prompt_ja":"歩道","canonical_snapshot":"sidewalk","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["sidewalk","pavement","footpath"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"pavement","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"英国英語でsidewalkに対応する主要語。地域variantとして実用性が高い。"},{"expression":"footpath","decision":"REJECT","reason":"歩行者用の道一般で、道路脇の「歩道」に限定されず範囲が広い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["pavement"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"US sidewalk / UK pavement の主要地域差を学ぶ価値が高い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01523","prompt_ja":"感情的な","canonical_snapshot":"emotional","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["emotional","sentimental","passionate"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"sentimental","decision":"REJECT","reason":"感傷的という特定の感情傾向を表し、一般の「感情的な」より狭い。"},{"expression":"passionate","decision":"REJECT","reason":"情熱的という肯定的・強い感情に偏り、一般promptには対応しない。"}],"after_paraphrases":[],"decision":"UNCHANGED","reason":"canonicalが一般的で、候補は特定の感情色に意味を狭める。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01524","prompt_ja":"傷つける","canonical_snapshot":"hurt","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["hurt","injure","wound"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"injure","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"身体を「傷つける」の主要動詞で、hurtとは別に重要な語彙価値がある。"},{"expression":"wound","decision":"REJECT","reason":"切創・銃創など外傷を与える意味に寄り、一般の「傷つける」には狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["injure"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"身体的損傷の主要語injureは有用だが、より限定的なwoundまでは登録しない。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01525","prompt_ja":"罪","canonical_snapshot":"sin","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["crime","sin","offense"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"crime","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"法的な「罪」の最も基本的な英語で、promptが区別しない主要senseとして回答価値が高い。"},{"expression":"offense","decision":"REJECT","reason":"法令違反・違反行為には成立するが、一般の「罪」への主要回答としてcrimeより狭い。"}],"after_paraphrases":["crime"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"promptは宗教・道徳上の罪と法的な罪を区別しないため、基本語crimeを追加する。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01526","prompt_ja":"そうでなければ","canonical_snapshot":"otherwise","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["otherwise","if not"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"if not","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「そうでなければ」を条件節として表す高頻度constructionで、会話でも重要。"}],"after_paraphrases":["if not"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"otherwiseとは構文の異なる主要な条件表現としてif notに独立価値がある。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01527","prompt_ja":"道徳的な","canonical_snapshot":"moral","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["moral","ethical"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"ethical","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「道徳的な／倫理的な」の主要語で、academic・businessでも重要。"}],"after_paraphrases":["ethical"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"moralとethicalは近接するがregister・使用領域が異なり、両方学ぶ価値が高い。"},{"entry_id":"vocab:01528","prompt_ja":"時間を守る","canonical_snapshot":"punctual","answers_snapshot":[],"existing_paraphrases":[],"blind_candidates":["be punctual","be on time","punctual"],"candidate_review":[{"expression":"be punctual","decision":"REJECT","reason":"canonicalにbeを付けただけの機械的surface variantで、paraphraseではない。"},{"expression":"be on time","decision":"ACCEPT","reason":"「時間を守る／時間どおりである」の最も基本的な句表現で、会話で高頻度。"}],"after_paraphrases":["be on time"],"decision":"CHANGED","reason":"表層variantは除外し、独立した高頻度construction be on timeを追加する。"}